          Rows.written_tree(~Tile.Tile8,cell,fresh,output)),
        Rows.written_length(~Tile.Tile8,cell,fresh,output))

# ---- The output piece of a window task ----

# The output tree a kind leaves after its segments.
def finish_tree(kind: Window.Sampling,+count: U32,+groups: U32,+kernel: U32,+parameters: Tree.Tree<Tile.Tile8>,tree: Tree.Tree<Tile.Tile8>) -> Tree.Tree<Tile.Tile8>:
  match kind:
    case Window.Pooling{pad}: tree
    case Window.Weighting{}: Updates.updated(~Tile.Tile8,~Rows.Weights,~Tile.Tile8,~bias_tap,~Tile.plus,U32.to_nat(count),0,Rows.Weights{parameters,kernel,groups},tree)

# An output piece and what a task holds after it.
type PieceModel<-Holder: Data,-value: Holder -> U32 -> Tile.Tile8,-holder: Holder,-computed: Window.Computed,-low: Nat,-high: Nat,-layout: Held.Spans,
  -parameters: Buffer.Model<Tile.Tile8>,-padding: TiledMap.Padding,-first: U32,-count: U32,-tree: Tree.Tree<Tile.Tile8>,-length: Nat> is Data:
  PieceModel{holding: Held.Holding<Tile.Tile8>,output: Buffer.Model<Tile.Tile8>,
    packed: {computed == Window.Computed{Partition.Leaf{TiledMap.padded(padding,first,count,Buffer.pack(~Tile.Tile8,output)),first,count,Unit{}},Held.pack(~Tile.Tile8,holding),Buffer.pack(~Tile.Tile8,parameters)} :
      Window.Computed},
